From fb29c0af6069ab6bd552f4f6ec71ba3e5680754c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 09:49:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath11k: tear down QMI when ahb probe fails after core
 init

ath11k_ahb_probe() calls ath11k_core_init() before it configures the
interrupts. ath11k_core_init() reaches ath11k_qmi_init_service(), which
registers the QMI service and starts ath11k_qmi_driver_event_work(), so
from that point a workqueue holds a reference to ab and the firmware
handshake is running.

If ath11k_ahb_config_irq() then fails, the error path jumps to
err_ce_free, which frees the CE pipes, the SRNGs and the smp2p handle
and ends in ath11k_core_free(ab) - without ever calling
ath11k_qmi_deinit_service(). The QMI work keeps running on freed memory:

  ath11k c000000.wifi: failed to configure irq: -16
  ath11k c000000.wifi: probe with driver ath11k failed with error -16
  platform c000000.wifi: chip_id 0x0 chip_family 0x4 board_id 0xff
  platform c000000.wifi: fw_version 0x270206d0 fw_build_timestamp ...
  Unable to handle kernel read from unreadable memory at virtual address 166

The prefix changing from "ath11k c000000.wifi:" to "platform
c000000.wifi:" is the driver detaching while its own work carries on.

Undo what ath11k_core_init() set up before the memory it works on goes
away, using the same sequence ath11k_ahb_remove() already uses for a
device whose QMI never came up: cancel the work, power the target down,
destroy the soc debugfs, release the QMI service and unregister the PM
notifier. ath11k_core_deinit() is not the right call here - it tears
down a fully started device and would stop pdevs and a firmware that
this path never created.

ath11k_pci_probe() does not have the problem: ath11k_pcic_config_irq()
runs before ath11k_core_init() there, and the failure paths after it
unwind in order.

Found while reading a crash report from an IPQ5018 board whose QCN6122
lost an interrupt request to a PCIe modem driver (OpenWrt forum thread
252655); reproduced and tested on a GL-B3000 by injecting a failure into
ath11k_ahb_config_irq() and rebinding a wifi device - the box panics
without this change and logs a clean probe failure with it.

Signed-off-by: Stanislaw Pal <kuncy7@gmail.com>
[Andrei: Ported to 7.2: the probe error path has no rproc deconfiguration step there; the new teardown runs before err_ce_free.]
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c | 11 ++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
index 72159496c..4db3338f4 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -1173,6 +1173,8 @@ static int ath11k_ahb_fw_resource_deinit(struct ath11k_base *ab)
 	return 0;
 }
 
+static void ath11k_ahb_remove_prepare(struct ath11k_base *ab);
+
 static int ath11k_ahb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	struct ath11k_base *ab;
@@ -1275,13 +1277,20 @@ static int ath11k_ahb_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	ret = ath11k_ahb_config_irq(ab);
 	if (ret) {
 		ath11k_err(ab, "failed to configure irq: %d\n", ret);
-		goto err_ce_free;
+		goto err_core_stop;
 	}
 
 	ath11k_qmi_fwreset_from_cold_boot(ab);
 
 	return 0;
 
+err_core_stop:
+	ath11k_ahb_remove_prepare(ab);
+	ath11k_ahb_power_down(ab, false);
+	ath11k_debugfs_soc_destroy(ab);
+	ath11k_qmi_deinit_service(ab);
+	ath11k_core_pm_notifier_unregister(ab);
+
 err_ce_free:
 	ath11k_ce_free_pipes(ab);
 
